  {
   "wanted": "a thin steel speed-ring / sleeve washer sized to the 608's inner-ring face (~12.4 mm OD) to carry the axle clamp load",
   "blocked_by": "the hardware list only offers ISO 7089 plain washers (M8 = 16 mm OD), and a 16 mm washer overlaps the bearing's outer-ring face",
   "why": "a 12-13 mm washer would press the bearing's inner ring alone, leaving the outer ring free to spin with the wheel. Without one I had to print two collars and a spacer in PLA, which creep under the sustained clamp load and add parts."
  },
  {
   "wanted": "to measure the broken wheel and the door's hanger bracket",
   "blocked_by": "the person could only measure the bearings and the bolt's shank; the old wheel, the bracket's plate thickness and its axle hole came back unmeasured",
   "why": "the old wheel's true OD and width set the tread diameter that keeps the door at the right height, and the bracket's thickness sets the axle's stack height and therefore the bolt length. Both are now guessed."
  },
